The user set a rule for the venue. Ana, who lives in Lisbon, uses a wheelchair. Any venue we book must have:

- step-free access from the car to the entrance;
- at least one accessible bedroom and bathroom on the ground floor;
- a work room that she can reach without stairs;
- step-free shared spaces: dining, terrace, and the place of any activity.

We check this before we choose a venue, with photos and measurements from the venue. Many old Portuguese country houses (quintas) fail this check.

